Subject: WTF: RedBlackTree::remove() drops the removed node links

remove() left the removed node pointing at its former children. The
links are CheckedPtrs: when such a child was freed first,
WTF_OVERRIDE_DELETE_FOR_CHECKED_PTR zeroed and leaked it, and freeing
the removed node later decremented the zeroed count and crashed in
crashDueToCheckedPtrToDeadObject(). RunLoopGeneric keeps its timers in
this tree, so destroying timers (here a WebProcessProxy and its
ResponsivenessTimer after a WebProcess crash) killed the UI process.
diff --git a/Source/WTF/wtf/RedBlackTree.h b/Source/WTF/wtf/RedBlackTree.h
index 3a122a4d9..a198defd0 100644
--- a/Source/WTF/wtf/RedBlackTree.h
+++ b/Source/WTF/wtf/RedBlackTree.h
@@ -286,6 +286,17 @@ public:
         } else if (y->color() == Black)
             removeFixup(x, xParent);
 
+#if defined(PS5_HOMEBREW)
+        // Drop the removed node's links. Its CheckedPtrs to its former
+        // children otherwise outlive the removal: when such a child is freed
+        // first, WTF_OVERRIDE_DELETE_FOR_CHECKED_PTR zeroes and leaks it, and
+        // destroying z later decrements the zeroed count, which crashes
+        // (crashDueToCheckedPtrToDeadObject). RunLoopGeneric's timer tree hit
+        // this when a WebProcessProxy and its ResponsivenessTimer went away.
+        z->setLeft(nullptr);
+        z->setRight(nullptr);
+        z->setParent(nullptr);
+#endif
         return z;
     }
     
